    "title": "kspec task patch appears to hang indefinitely — had to kill and use task set + task note as workarou",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "**What**: `kspec task patch @ref` hangs indefinitely when invoked without piped stdin and without `--data`. The command reads from `process.stdin` using a `for await` loop (line 999-1003 in `src/cli/commands/task.ts`) which blocks forever waiting for input when stdin is a TTY. **Where**: `src/cli/commands/task.ts`, lines 993-1004 — the `else` branch of the `if (options.data)` check. When `--data` is not provided, the code does `for await (const chunk of process.stdin)` which never resolves if stdin is a terminal. **How**: Add TTY detection before attempting to read stdin. If `process.stdin.isTTY` is true and `--data` was not provided, print an error message explaining that either `--data <json>` must be provided or JSON must be piped to stdin, then exit with a validation error. Example: `if (!options.data && process.stdin.isTTY) { error('Provide --data or pipe JSON to stdin'); process.exit(EXIT_CODES.VALIDATION_FAILED); }`. Alternatively, add a short timeout on stdin reads. **Done when**: (1) Running `kspec task patch @ref` without `--data` and without piped stdin immediately prints a helpful error and exits. (2) `kspec task patch @ref --data '{...}'` still works. (3) `echo '{...}' | kspec task patch @ref` still works. (4) Batch exec engine (`src/cli/batch-exec.ts`) still works with task patch.",
