    "title": "Fix @observations slug ambiguity — kspec validate reports 6 errors for duplicate slug. Pre-existing ",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "**What**: `kspec validate` reports 6 reference errors because the slug `observations` maps to two different items: a spec feature (ULID `01KF1XFBK00000000000000000`, type feature in `modules/meta.yaml`) and a skill (ULID `01KJ51SSZ2NVZGXE32NR5TWPS9`, type skill in `kynetic.meta.yaml`). Any `@observations` reference is ambiguous. 6 references in `modules/meta.yaml` (implements fields) and `project.tasks.yaml` (spec_ref) are affected. **Where**: `.kspec/modules/meta.yaml` — the spec feature item with slug `observations`. `.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml` — the skill with id `observations`. The slug collision happens in the reference index (`src/parser/refs.ts`) which treats spec slugs and meta item ids as the same namespace. **How**: Rename the skill id from `observations` to something distinct like `observe` or `capture-observations`, OR rename the spec feature slug. The skill id is less entrenched (it was recently created) so renaming it is lower risk. Update: (1) the skill id in `kynetic.meta.yaml`, (2) any skill file references, (3) the rendered skill in `.claude/skills/`. After the rename, `kspec validate` should report 0 reference errors for this slug. Use `kspec batch` for the meta changes. **Done when**: (1) `kspec validate` no longer reports duplicate slug errors for `@observations`. (2) The skill is still functional under its new id. (3) All 6 previously-ambiguous references resolve correctly. (4) `kspec agents generate` still includes the observations skill.",
