    "_ulid": "01KJDQ139SP70H2H9GNBH8BM72",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "kspec agents generate should include package version in content hash (or add --force flag) so versio",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "**What**: `kspec agents generate` skips regeneration when content is unchanged, but the staleness check does not include the package version in the content hash. After a version bump (e.g., 0.6.0 to 0.7.0), the generated file header comment is stale, but the hash matches because version is not part of the hash input. **Where**: `src/cli/commands/agents.ts` — the `computeMetaHash()` function (line 125-154) computes a hash from skills, conventions, workflows, and template sections, but does not include the package version. The `generateFreshnessComment()` function (line 160) uses `version` from the package but this is only in the output, not the hash. The skip logic is at ~line 346-348 where `checkAgentStatus()` compares the stored hash. **How**: Add the package `version` string to the hash input in `computeMetaHash()`. Add `data.version = version` (importing `version` from the package, which is already imported at the top of the file for `generateFreshnessComment`). This way, any version bump automatically invalidates the hash and triggers regeneration. Alternatively or additionally, add a `--force` flag to `kspec agents generate` that bypasses the hash check. **Done when**: (1) `computeMetaHash()` includes the package version in its hash computation. (2) After a version bump, `kspec agents generate` regenerates the file instead of skipping. (3) Existing tests in `tests/agents-instruction-gen.test.ts` updated to reflect the new hash behavior. (4) Optionally: `--force` flag added to bypass the hash check entirely.",
